course: dictionary
lesson: 8014
title: Many meanings of refer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Refer is a word with more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one to use. «Don't ever refer to it again, please.» Here refer to means talk about it. The speaker wants the topic dropped.
explain: In school, «refer to page 10» means look at page 10 for information. In maths, «this refers to the number of apples» means the letter or number stands for that number. Each time, ask: what does the sentence want me to do or understand?
explain: «A GP refers people to specialists if needed.» Here refer means send someone to another person or place for help. The GP is not talking about the specialists. The GP is sending the patient to them.
explain: A quick check helps. Swap in a simpler word such as talk about, look at, send, or stand for. If one of them fits the sentence, you have found the meaning.
fact: Refer is a verb. Its forms are refers, referred, and referring.
fact: To refer to someone or something means to talk or write about them.
fact: To refer to a book, map or list means to look at it for information.
fact: To refer someone to another person or place means to send them there for help.
fact: «A specialist is a doctor who focuses on one part of the body or one kind of illness.» Being referred to a specialist does not mean something terrible is wrong.
exercise: «Don't ever refer to it again, please.» What does refer to mean here? | *Talk about | Look up in a book | Spell out letter by letter | Send somewhere for help
exercise: Mrs Patel says, «Refer to page 10.» What should you do? | *Look at page 10 for the information | Read only page 1 | Throw the book away | Draw a picture of page 10
exercise: In maths, «this refers to the number of apples». What does this do? | *It stands for the number of apples | It adds two apples to the total | It is a question to answer | It is the name of a fruit shop
test: «A GP refers people to specialists if needed.» What does refers people to mean? | Looks at a list of specialists | Talks about people who work with specialists | *Sends people to specialists for help | Makes people feel better straight away
test: Being referred to a specialist means what? | Something terrible is definitely wrong | *It does not mean something terrible is wrong | You have broken a bone | You must stay at home forever
exam: Which sentence uses refer to mean send someone somewhere for help? | *The GP will refer you to a specialist | The teacher said «refer to the table» | The dog referred to the park | Refer is a verb with four forms
